# Frontend Standards

## API Client Layer

- All API calls go through `client/src/api/` — never inline `fetch` in components
- Never hardcode backend URLs — always use `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`
- Custom hooks (`useTickets`, `useTicket`, `useUsers`) own: fetch + loading + error state
- Components own render only — zero business logic inside JSX

## Component Rules

- Handle **loading, error, and empty states** on every list and page
- Create reusable components in `components/common/`, `components/tickets/`, `components/comments/`
- Never enforce status transition rules in the UI — display hints only; backend is authoritative
- Show API `error.message` to the user near the relevant field (especially invalid transitions — AC-08)
- Display `"Unassigned"` when `assignedTo` is null
- Render user content as text — **never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`**
- Disable submit buttons while requests are in flight

## State & Routing

- Persist `search` and `status` filter in URL query params (`?search=...&status=Open`)
- Use React Router `BrowserRouter`; routes: `/`, `/tickets/new`, `/tickets/:id`
- Local component state for form inputs and UI toggles
- No global store (Redux/Zustand) — custom hooks are sufficient for v1

## Styling

- All styling via Tailwind CSS utility classes (see `tailwind-css.mdc`)
- Use `clsx` or `cn` for conditional class merging — never string concatenation
- Responsive via Tailwind prefixes (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`) — no custom media queries
